# TODO - User-supplied DOOM source interoperability generator

## Objective

After quality output is accepted, use `algorithms/diff/` a second time to learn a
source-bound deterministic amalgamation transform from the normalized multi-file
DOOM tree and a local accepted single-file oracle. A thin DOOM recipe will emit
`algorithms/doom/amalgamate/main.rs`; that transform will materialize one
canonical `algorithms/doom/amalgamate/out/doom_amalgamated.c`.

The generic diff engine does not replace semantic amalgamation validation. DOOM
and C-specific policy must still use pinned Clang evidence to resolve
translation-unit boundaries, internal linkage, preprocessing environments,
includes, declarations, and required provenance.

This stage is the planned second consumer of the source-bound diff generator. It
is also the source-level precursor to the later goal of compiling one portable
DOOM C artifact through the Malbolge pipeline.

## Acceptance

- Amalgamation consumes only accepted generated quality output and never rewrites
  the user-owned root source directly.
- The local single-file oracle is authoring evidence only and is not required by
  the emitted transform.
- Exact normalized baseline plus generated transform reproduces the accepted
  single-file oracle byte-for-byte.
- Translation-unit semantics, internal linkage, macro environments, declaration
  ordering, and required provenance survive deterministic aggregation.
- Plain textual concatenation and source-specific hand patches are not accepted
  implementations.
- The generated transform remains source-bound; transform bytes alone cannot
  materialize the single-file target.
- The normalized multi-file native build and the generated single-file native
  build are compared differentially before admission.
- The accepted `doom_amalgamated.c` is copied byte-for-byte to
  `tests/applications/doom/out/doom.c` for the end-to-end pipeline fixture.
- Repeated recipe generation and materialization are deterministic.
- Evidence is durable enough to move this TODO to `docs/todo/completed/`.

## Evidence

- Expected durable artifact surface: `algorithms/diff/`, the DOOM generator
  recipe, `algorithms/doom/amalgamate/main.rs`, and relevant contracts/tests.
- Local ignored evidence: accepted `quality/out/doom_fixed/`, the single-file
  oracle, `amalgamate/out/doom_amalgamated.c`, and application runtime outputs.
- Required evidence: exact reconstruction hashes, normalized/amalgamated
  manifests, Clang semantic/provenance mapping, native differential traces,
  source-binding rejection tests, and Jig.
- Prerequisite completion evidence: `doom-quality-and-modernization-pass`,
  `source-bound-diff-generator`, `clang-c-frontend-integration`, and the
  legal/provenance corpus.
